# =============================================================================
# Dockerfile Misconfigurations - Accepted Risks
# =============================================================================
# These are Trivy misconfiguration checks that are intentionally accepted.
#
# NOTE (2026-10-04 re-audit): this section was rewritten against the scanner CI
# actually runs, because both entries' rationales had come false. Measured with
# aquasec/trivy:0.74.0 — the exact pin at .github/workflows/trivy.yml:280 —
# running the same repo-wide config scan as CI (trivy.yml:93-108, severity
# CRITICAL,HIGH,MEDIUM, exit-code 1):
#   AVD-DS-0001 deleted: removing the ID reveals NOTHING. It suppressed zero
#     findings, and its stated premise is gone — no FROM line in the repo builds
#     FROM nemotron-base anymore, and the docker checks do not flag :latest on a
#     COPY --from= (see REMOVED).
#   AVD-DS-0002 kept, rationale corrected: deleting ONLY this ID surfaces five
#     HIGH "no USER directive" findings, and none of them is the file the old
#     comment described (see the attribution list below, and REMOVED).
# One ID covering five files is forced, not sloppy: these checks report at FILE
# level with no line number, and per-file scoping does not exist for config
# scans — measured, each attempt still returned all five findings: INI-section
# ignore files with ids+paths (both ID spellings, AVD-DS-0002 and DS-0002), glob
# paths, paths=["*"], and an inline "# trivy:ignore:AVD-DS-0002" comment. So the
# honest lever is the rationale below, not a narrower ignore.

# AVD-DS-0002 - no USER directive (non-root) in four image definitions (REVIEW BY: 2027-07-05)
# Attributed by deleting this ID alone and re-running the CI-pinned scanner
# (trivy 0.74.0, repo-wide config scan, 2026-10-04: FIVE findings then; O1.5
# (UR-19, 2026-10-09) deleted the fifth file — the archive's Dockerfile.yolo26-benchmark,
# "ARCHIVED, built by nobody" below — with the archive itself, so a register
# naming it would name a path that no longer exists. Four remain, and the
# measured reason each is deferred rather than fixed:
#   docker/base.Dockerfile                  PUBLISHED BASE IMAGE. Every layer
#     needs root (apt-get install; uv pip install --system writes
#     /usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages; the cache mount is literally
#     /root/.cache/uv). A base that ends in USER forces non-root on every
#     consumer, whose first instruction is apt-get — a base image with USER is a
#     broken base, not a hardened one.
#   docker/python-freethreaded/Dockerfile   PUBLISHED BASE IMAGE, same class and
#     stronger: it mirrors the official python Dockerfile (build-from-source
#     configure/make install, ldconfig, apt-mark/purge, symlinks into
#     /usr/local/bin). It is published under a python-lookalike name precisely so
#     third parties FROM it, so an in-image USER is a semantic change to an
#     advertised public base. Guarded against silent misuse by
#     TestNoRepoConsumerOfPublishedBases.
#   synthbench/generate/comfy/Containerfile  NOT FIXABLE THIS WAY, measured. It
#     runs under ROOTLESS podman with no --user
#     (synthbench/generate/comfy/serve.py:106-136), so container root already
#     maps to the invoking host UID — which is exactly why its two read-write
#     HOST binds, {out_dir}:/opt/ComfyUI/output and {cache_dir}:/root/.cache
#     (serve.py:131,133, both created by that same host user at serve.py:151-153)
#     are writable today. An in-image USER remaps that to a different sub-UID
#     inside the userns and strands the mounts, plus ComfyUI's own writes inside
#     /opt/ComfyUI. The correct lever is run-time --user, not a Dockerfile USER.
#   ai/gateway/Dockerfile                   DEFERRED WITH A FIX RECIPE (owner
#     decision, 2026-10-04). This one IS a genuine hardening win and the only
#     service image in the set. Recipe: mirror the in-repo precedent
#     ai/vlm/Dockerfile:94-136 (groupadd/useradd uid 1000, chown the dirs, USER
#     last) AND (a) build-time chown of the image-baked /models/repository, which
#     three runtime writers mutate — ai/gateway/patch_triton_configs.py:130
#     write_text, ai/gateway/entrypoint.sh:109-110 rm -rf + ln -sf,
#     ai/gateway/residency.py:114-133 rmtree/move (deliberately no "|| true", so a
#     permission failure stops the container — loud, not silent); (b) host-side
#     ownership of the read-write bind ${AI_MODELS_PATH:-/export/ai_models}/triton:
#     /models/cache and of the HF cache bind, since the service runs with
#     cap_drop [ALL] + no-new-privileges and cannot fix ownership from inside;
#     (c) move the /root/.nv + /root/.cache/huggingface volume mounts off root's
#     home. Must be validated live on the GPU box: NO CI job builds this image
#     (deploy.yml's matrix is backend+frontend only, ci.yml:1889-1901), so nothing
#     here can prove it.
# Deliberately NOT a fix here: adding USER to the two bases or to comfy would
# satisfy the scanner while breaking real builds. Guard:
# TestMisconfigIgnoreNamesRealTargets (the ID's rationale must keep naming these
# four, and must not re-claim the file the old comment described).
AVD-DS-0002

